{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls source_evidence; nl -ba source_evidence/selected_model.py | sed -n '1,190p'\"","aggregated_output":"data_manifest.json\ndevelopment_gaussian.py\ndevelopment_joint.py\nevaluate_final.py\nfinal_manifest.json\nrequirements.txt\nselected_model.py\nselected_spec.toml\ntask_contract.json\n     1\t\"\"\"Deterministic training-only rank-selected local-moment ILR regression.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe incumbent centers and base scales are unchanged. Three outer training folds\n     4\tselect the existing scalar scale correction using nested residual tables and\n     5\tswapped held-out pseudo-calibration/evaluation halves. Selection minimizes a\n     6\trow-weighted, alpha-averaged log arithmetic mean ILR-box volume, not simplex\n     7\tvolume. Unavailable finite-sample ranks or invalid radii fall back to the original\n     8\tGaussian selector for the entire fit. Fewer than five training rows retain its\n     9\texact neutral correction. Independent evaluator calibration is untouched; no\n    10\tconditional or covariate-shift coverage guarantee is added.\n    11\t\n    12\tInterface: handle(request: dict) -> dict, finite JSON only, no extra response keys.\n    13\tKeep the entrypoint self-contained in this file; native validation stages only this\n    14\tfile plus installed packages, with a read-only filesystem and memory-only state.\n    15\tEvery request has exactly the keys shown below. Seed is any int in [0,2**63);\n    16\tit initializes randomness and NEVER chooses a workload. No paths are accepted.\n    17\t\n    18\tOperations/state transitions:\n    19\t  reset: {op:'reset', seed:int} -> {ok:true}; clears ALL state, enters unfitted.\n    20\t  predict: {op:'predict', x:array} -> {status:'unfitted'} until fit_scale completes.\n    21\t    When fitted: {center:array, scale:array}, both shape [N,K-1], finite float64;\n    22\t    center is in the fixed ILR basis, abs(center)<=100; scale in [1e-4,100].\n    23\t    Read-only, deterministic for equal inputs; identical rows have equal outputs.\n    24\t  fit_center: {op:'fit_center', x:array, y:array, dimension:int} -> {ok:true}.\n    25\t    X [N,6], Y [N,K], K in {3,8}, positive rows summing to 1, training only.\n    26\t    Fits center; invalidates scale, enters center-fitted but still unfitted.\n    27\t  fit_scale: {op:'fit_scale'} -> {ok:true}; requires fit_center, uses retained\n    28\t    TRAINING residuals only, enters fitted. No calibration/test labels provided.\n    29\t\n    30\tArray schema (exact keys): {encoding:'base64', dtype:'float64', byte_order:'little',\n    31\t  shape:[rows,columns], data:ASCII base64 of C-order little-endian float64 bytes}.\n    32\t1<=N<=4096, columns<=8, each logical array <=1 MiB. Complete request/response\n    33\tincluding envelope and newline must be <2 MiB (and strictly <64 MiB harness cap).\n    34\tNo state transfer or chunk operations exist: declared maximum shapes all fit inline;\n    35\tlarger logical inputs are rejected, never written to disk. Live model state <64 MiB.\n    36\tAdditional keys, nonfinite numbers, malformed encodings, and invalid state transitions\n    37\tare errors, not diagnostics. Responses contain no optional keys or internal reports.\n    38\t\n    39\tBasis convention: column j-1 (j=1..K-1) has first j entries 1/sqrt(j*(j+1)),\n    40\tentry j equal to -j/sqrt(j*(j+1)), remaining entries zero. z=log(y) @ basis.\n    41\tInverse softmax(z @ basis.T). Evaluator owns calibration and region membership:\n    42\tmax(abs(z-center)/scale) <= independent split-conformal order statistic, separately\n    43\tat alpha=.05,.10,.20. Targets to predict are observed continuous compositions,\n    44\tnot labels or latent categorical probabilities. Prediction queries do not identify\n    45\tcalibration/test membership, alpha, case, plane, targets, scores, or baselines.\n    46\t\n    47\tPublic workload: six continuous X features; K=3 or 8; logistic-normal IID,\n    48\theteroscedastic Dirichlet IID and covariate-shift stress. Training-only fitting can\n    49\tbe replaced within this exact output family. Evaluator also tests constant-input,\n    50\tnonidentity-permuted-input, zero-radius copy-point, and reset/unfitted controls.\n    51\tNo superiority or realized-coverage threshold is a search eligibility requirement.\n    52\t\"\"\"\n    53\t\n    54\timport base64\n    55\timport math\n    56\t\n    57\timport numpy as np\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t_state = {}\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef _decode(value):\n    64\t    if type(value) is not dict or set(value) != {\n    65\t        'encoding', 'dtype', 'byte_order', 'shape', 'data'\n    66\t    }:\n    67\t        raise ValueError('invalid array schema')\n    68\t    shape = value['shape']\n    69\t    if (value['encoding'] != 'base64' or value['dtype'] != 'float64'\n    70\t            or value['byte_order'] != 'little' or type(shape) is not list\n    71\t            or len(shape) != 2 or any(type(size) is not int for size in shape)\n    72\t            or not 1 <= shape[0] <= 4096 or not 1 <= shape[1] <= 8):\n    73\t        raise ValueError('invalid array metadata')\n    74\t    raw = base64.b64decode(value['data'], validate=True)\n    75\t    if len(raw) != math.prod(shape) * 8 or len(raw) > 1024 * 1024:\n    76\t        raise ValueError('invalid array size')\n    77\t    result = np.frombuffer(raw, dtype='<f8').reshape(shape).copy()\n    78\t    if not np.isfinite(result).all():\n    79\t        raise ValueError('nonfinite array')\n    80\t    return result\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef _encode(array):\n    84\t    array = np.ascontiguousarray(array, dtype='<f8')\n    85\t    return {'encoding': 'base64', 'dtype': 'float64', 'byte_order': 'little',\n    86\t            'shape': list(array.shape), 'data': base64.b64encode(array.tobytes()).decode('ascii')}\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef _basis(dimension):\n    90\t    basis = np.zeros((dimension, dimension - 1))\n    91\t    for column in range(1, dimension):\n    92\t        denominator = math.sqrt(column * (column + 1))\n    93\t        basis[:column, column - 1] = 1 / denominator\n    94\t        basis[column, column - 1] = -column / denominator\n    95\t    return basis\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tdef _features(features):\n    99\t    return np.column_stack((np.ones(len(features)), features, features ** 2,\n   100\t                            np.sin(features), features[:, 0] * features[:, 1]))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef _ridge(features, targets, penalty):\n   104\t    regularizer = np.eye(features.shape[1]) * penalty\n   105\t    regularizer[0, 0] = 1e-8\n   106\t    return np.linalg.solve(features.T @ features + regularizer, features.T @ targets)\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef _training_folds(sample_count):\n   110\t    indices = np.random.default_rng(0).permutation(sample_count)\n   111\t    return np.array_split(indices, 3)\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\tdef _fit_incumbent(train_features, train_targets):\n   115\t    design = _features(train_features)\n   116\t    ilr_targets = np.log(train_targets) @ _basis(train_targets.shape[1])\n   117\t    coefficient = _ridge(design, ilr_targets, 1.0)\n   118\t    residual = ilr_targets - design @ coefficient\n   119\t    log_residual = np.log(np.maximum(abs(residual), .02))\n   120\t    scale_coefficient = _ridge(design, log_residual, 10.0)\n   121\t    return coefficient, scale_coefficient\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\tdef _incumbent_predictions(model, features):\n   125\t    coefficient, scale_coefficient = model\n   126\t    design = _features(features)\n   127\t    base_centers = np.clip(design @ coefficient, -100, 100)\n   128\t    base_scales = np.clip(np.exp(np.clip(design @ scale_coefficient,\n   129\t                                        math.log(1e-4), math.log(100))), 1e-4, 100)\n   130\t    return base_centers, base_scales\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\tdef build_oof_residual_table(train_features, train_targets):\n   134\t    ilr_targets = np.log(train_targets) @ _basis(train_targets.shape[1])\n   135\t    oof_centers = np.empty_like(ilr_targets)\n   136\t    oof_scales = np.empty_like(ilr_targets)\n   137\t    all_indices = np.arange(len(train_features))\n   138\t    for valid_indices in _training_folds(len(train_features)):\n   139\t        fit_indices = np.setdiff1d(all_indices, valid_indices)\n   140\t        assert np.intersect1d(fit_indices, valid_indices).size == 0\n   141\t        model = _fit_incumbent(train_features[fit_indices], train_targets[fit_indices])\n   142\t        oof_centers[valid_indices], oof_scales[valid_indices] = _incumbent_predictions(\n   143\t            model, train_features[valid_indices])\n   144\t    scale_floor = 1e-4\n   145\t    standardized_residuals = (ilr_targets - oof_centers) / np.maximum(oof_scales, scale_floor)\n   146\t    relative_squared_residuals = np.mean(standardized_residuals ** 2, axis=1)\n   147\t    location = np.mean(train_features, axis=0)\n   148\t    spread = np.maximum(np.std(train_features, axis=0), 1e-8)\n   149\t    return {'features': (train_features - location) / spread,\n   150\t            'location': location, 'spread': spread,\n   151\t            'relative_squared_residuals': relative_squared_residuals}\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\tdef _local_moment_ratio(residual_table, query_features, bandwidth, prior_mass):\n   155\t    assert bandwidth > 0.0 and prior_mass > 0.0\n   156\t    reference_features = residual_table['features']\n   157\t    relative_squared_residuals = residual_table['relative_squared_residuals']\n   158\t    reference_norms = np.sum(reference_features ** 2, axis=1)\n   159\t    ratios = np.empty(len(query_features), dtype=np.float64)\n   160\t    for start in range(0, len(query_features), 128):\n   161\t        query = ((query_features[start:start + 128] - residual_table['location'])\n   162\t                 / residual_table['spread'])\n   163\t        squared_distances = np.maximum(\n   164\t            np.sum(query ** 2, axis=1)[:, None] + reference_norms[None, :]\n   165\t            - 2.0 * (query @ reference_features.T), 0.0)\n   166\t        weights = np.exp(-0.5 * squared_distances / (bandwidth ** 2))\n   167\t        moment_ratio = (weights @ relative_squared_residuals + prior_mass) / (weights.sum(axis=1) + prior_mass)\n   168\t        ratios[start:start + len(query)] = moment_ratio\n   169\t    return ratios\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\tdef apply_scale_correction(base_scales, moment_ratio, blend):\n   173\t    if blend == 0.0: return base_scales.copy()\n   174\t    correction = np.exp(0.5 * blend * np.log(np.clip(moment_ratio, 0.25, 4.0)))\n   175\t    lower_factor = np.max(1e-4 / base_scales, axis=1)\n   176\t    upper_factor = np.min(100.0 / base_scales, axis=1)\n   177\t    correction = np.clip(correction, lower_factor, upper_factor)\n   178\t    below_floor = np.any(base_scales * correction[:, None] < 1e-4, axis=1)\n   179\t    above_ceiling = np.any(base_scales * correction[:, None] > 100.0, axis=1)\n   180\t    correction[below_floor] = np.nextafter(lower_factor[below_floor], np.inf)\n   181\t    correction[above_ceiling] = np.nextafter(upper_factor[above_ceiling], 0.0)\n   182\t    adjusted_scales = base_scales * correction[:, None]\n   183\t    assert np.all(np.isfinite(adjusted_scales)) and np.all(adjusted_scales > 0.0)\n   184\t    assert np.all(adjusted_scales >= 1e-4) and np.all(adjusted_scales <= 100.0)\n   185\t    return adjusted_scales\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\tdef _select_correction_gaussian(train_features, train_targets):\n   189\t    candidate_blends = (0.0, 0.5, 1.0)\n   190\t    feature_dimension = train_features.shape[1]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
