{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat literature/FanSesia2025.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"title\": \"Interpretable Multivariate Conformal Prediction with Fast Transductive Standardization\",\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Yunjie Fan\",\n    \"Matteo Sesia\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": 2025,\n  \"arxiv_id\": \"2512.15383\",\n  \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.15383\",\n  \"accessed_at\": \"2026-11-17T14:24:21.314151+00:00\",\n  \"discovery_artifact\": \"references.openalex.json\",\n  \"discovery_source_id\": \"ref.openalex.W7116099311\",\n  \"excerpts\": {\n    \"absolute_residuals\": \"We assume access to a pre-trained joint predictive model f ^ = ( f ^ 1 , … , f ^ d ) \\\\hat{f}=(\\\\hat{f}_{1},\\\\ldots,\\\\hat{f}_{d}) , fitted on data independent of both the calibration set 𝒟 cal \\\\mathcal{D}_{\\\\mathrm{cal}} and the test point.\\nThis model is treated as a “black-box” and could be anything; the only requirement for f ^ \\\\hat{f} is that it must provide us with a coordinate-wise generalized residual function E : 𝒳 × ℝ d → ℝ d , E:\\\\mathcal{X}\\\\times\\\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\\\to\\\\mathbb{R}^{d}, which aims to quantify the model’s prediction error along each output dimension.\\nApplying this function to a data point ( X , Y ) (X,Y) produces the vector E ⁡ ( X , Y ) = ( E 1 ​ ( X , Y ) , … , E d ​ ( X , Y ) ) E(X,Y)=\\\\bigl(E_{1}(X,Y),\\\\ldots,E_{d}(X,Y)\\\\bigr) .\",\n    \"algorithms_S1_S2\": {\n      \"alg1a\": \"Algorithm S1 Separate Prediction Intervals with Bonferroni Correction Input: Calibration residuals { E i } i = 1 n \\\\{E^{i}\\\\}_{i=1}^{n} ; target miscoverage level α ∈ ( 0 , 1 ) \\\\alpha\\\\in(0,1) ; test input X n + 1 X^{n+1} . 1: Compute α ∗ ← α / d \\\\alpha^{*}\\\\leftarrow\\\\alpha/d . 2: for j = 1 j=1 to d d do 3: Compute Q ^ 1 − α ∗ , j ← Q ^ 1 − α ∗ ​ ( E j 1 , … , E j n ) \\\\hat{Q}_{1-\\\\alpha^{*},j}\\\\leftarrow\\\\hat{Q}_{1-\\\\alpha^{*}}(E^{1}_{j},\\\\ldots,E^{n}_{j}) . 4: end for 5: return C ^ Bonf . ( X n + 1 ) ← { y ∈ ℝ d : 0 ≤ E j ( X n + 1 , y ) ≤ Q ^ 1 − α ∗ , j , ∀ j ∈ [ d ] } \\\\hat{C}^{\\\\mathrm{Bonf.}}(X^{n+1})\\\\leftarrow\\\\left\\\\{y\\\\in\\\\mathbb{R}^{d}:0\\\\leq E_{j}(X^{n+1},y)\\\\leq\\\\hat{Q}_{1-\\\\alpha^{*},j},\\\\forall j\\\\in[d]\\\\right\\\\} .\",\n      \"alg2a\": \"Algorithm S2 Prediction Intervals via Dimension Reduction with ℓ ∞ \\\\ell_{\\\\infty} -Norm (Unscaled) Input: Calibration residuals { E i } i = 1 n \\\\{E^{i}\\\\}_{i=1}^{n} ; target miscoverage level α ∈ ( 0 , 1 ) \\\\alpha\\\\in(0,1) ; test input X n + 1 X^{n+1} . 1: Compute S unscaled i ← ‖ E i ‖ ∞ S^{i}_{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}}\\\\leftarrow\\\\|E^{i}\\\\|_{\\\\infty} for i = 1 , … , n i=1,\\\\ldots,n . 2: Compute Q ^ 1 − α unscaled ← Q ^ 1 − α ​ ( S unscaled 1 , … , S unscaled n ) \\\\hat{Q}^{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}}_{1-\\\\alpha}\\\\leftarrow\\\\hat{Q}_{1-\\\\alpha}(S^{1}_{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}},\\\\dots,S^{n}_{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}}) 3: return C ^ unscaled ( X n + 1 ) ← { y ∈ ℝ d : 0 ≤ E j n + 1 ( y ) ≤ Q ^ 1 − α unscaled , ∀ j ∈ [ d ] } \\\\hat{C}^{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}}(X^{n+1})\\\\leftarrow\\\\left\\\\{y\\\\in\\\\mathbb{R}^{d}:0\\\\leq E^{n+1}_{j}(y)\\\\leq\\\\hat{Q}^{\\\\mathrm{unscaled}}_{1-\\\\alpha},\\\\forall j\\\\in[d]\\\\right\\\\} .\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"read_scope\": \"Selected introductory comparator paragraphs; Sections 2.3, 2.4 and 2.6; Appendix A.1 Algorithms S1 and S2. Bibliography removed before text inspection. No citation links followed.\",\n  \"supported_context\": \"Algorithm S1 calibrates each residual coordinate at alpha/d; Algorithm S2 calibrates the infinity norm of nonnegative residual vectors at alpha. Absolute regression residuals are allowed in Section 2.3. These support general vector-response comparator context, not attribution of the simplex intersection, exact evaluated source identity, or superiority.\",\n  \"restriction_audit\": \"Only the directly retrieved multivariate comparator paper was consulted. No joint compositional-conformal discovery, citation traversal, or prohibited content was identified or used.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
