_02_shrunk_local_moment_scaling_attempt_01\", \"combined_score\": 0.6421289430111841, \"correct\": true, \"eligible\": true, \"eval_index\": 2, \"idea_dir_name\": \"02_training_only_shrunk_local_moment_scale_correction\", \"idea_id\": \"cycle_02_shrunk_local_moment_scaling\", \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation/ideas/02_training_only_shrunk_local_moment_scale_correction/program_1\", \"program_id\": \"program_1\", \"program_idx\": 1}\nkeys ['attempt_dir_name', 'attempt_id', 'combined_score', 'correct', 'eligible', 'eval_index', 'evaluation_evidence', 'idea_dir_name', 'idea_id', 'program_dir', 'program_id', 'program_idx']\n{\"attempt_dir_name\": \"idea_root\", \"attempt_id\": \"cycle_03_rank_calibrated_scale_selection_attempt_01\", \"combined_score\": 0.6450635814905741, \"correct\": true, \"eligible\": true, \"eval_index\": 3, \"idea_dir_name\": \"03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection\", \"idea_id\": \"cycle_03_rank_calibrated_scale_selection\", \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1\", \"program_id\": \"program_1\", \"program_idx\": 1}\nevidence_sources dict\nresult.top_program_01 {\"attempt_id\": \"cycle_03_rank_calibrated_scale_selection_attempt_01\", \"id\": \"result.top_program_01\", \"idea_id\": \"cycle_03_rank_calibrated_scale_selection\", \"program_dir\": \"work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation/ideas/03_training_only_conformal_rank_scale_selection/program_1\", \"program_id\": \"program_1\", \"type\": \"metric\", \"value\": 0.6450635814905741}\n    feasible = False\n    rpc = None\n    failed = None\n    try:\n        if np.__version__ != '1.26.4' or sys.version_info[:2] not in ((3, 11), (3, 12)):\n            raise RuntimeError('requires NumPy 1.26.4 on CPython 3.11 or 3.12')\n        preflight()\n        root = Path(os.environ.get('TASK_SOURCE_DIR', str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))) / 'resources' / PLANE\n        episodes = load_resources(root, smoke, hard_deadline - FINISH_RESERVE)\n        expected = [SEEDS[0]] if smoke else [seed for seed in SEEDS for _case in CASES]\n        if [episode['seed'] for episode in episodes] != expected:\n            raise ValueError('reset transcript mismatch')\n        rpc = RPC(arguments.program_path, WALL_SECONDS)\n        outcomes, complete = run_declared_episodes(episodes, hard_deadline=hard_deadline,\n            finish_reserve=FINISH_RESERVE, reset_timeout=RESET_TIMEOUT, episode_overhead=EPISODE_OVERHEAD,\n            rpc_cap=WORK_SECONDS, clock=time.monotonic, rpc=rpc, evaluate=evaluate_episode,\n            worst_case=worst_case, record_failure=record_failure)\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e8cc2efa334e69b5e59cec03ddcdd75b097f2d59336988b391cd3a092ecb18f1\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Controlled evaluation of heteroscedastic, isometric-logratio split-conformal regions for continuous compositional regression\",\n    \"description\": \"Scientific target: observed positive continuous compositional regression, not classification labels or latent probabilities. Synthetic-only controlled scaled-ILR split conformal; null and negative results valid. Linux x86-64 with Landlock ABI>=3 and libseccomp.so.2 required for native smoke; production uses harness no-network candidate container. Native validation stages only the supplied self-contained entrypoint (<=32MiB), never sibling directories that could contain evaluator data. Candidate implementations must stay self-contained in their entrypoint. Native candidate filesystem is read-only (code and runtime libraries only), with private-data/proc denial, no networking or subprocesses, own-thread-only signals/limits, fixed CPU affinity and no filesystem-persistent state across resets. CPython 3.11 or 3.12 with NumPy 1.26.4 (3.12 actually validated), CPU only. Aggregate 8 cores/16GiB partitioned evaluator4/8GiB and candidate4/8GiB; four BLAS threads and all-thread CPU limits 4800s/role search and14400s/role final; no paid API, GPU, or external asset. Total storage<10GB and one-week research limit. No task-local publication controller or telemetry accessor.\\nFrozen generator composition-v1 is executable generate_arrays in each evaluator: six features uniform[-1.5,1.5], or shifted TEST only clipped Normal(.8,1) in[-2.5,3]; logistic-normal sigma=.25; Dirichlet conditional concentration 4+35/(1+exp(2*x0)), gamma floor1e-12 then closure; subgroup x0>0 vs<=0. Mean and fixed Helmert ILR basis are in evaluator; conditional law unchanged under shift. Case order LN_IID_K3,LN_IID_K8,DIR_IID_K3,DIR_IID_K8,DIR_SHIFT_K3,DIR_SHIFT_K8, seed-major. Search sizes512/256/1024 train/cal/test; final1024/512/2048;128 frozen contexts,1024 uniform-simplex probes. Smoke first case/seed only,64/32/64 rows,16contexts64probes, same loading/RPC/fitting/scoring/control/aggregation path, <=120s. No replay or auxiliary reset episodes.\\nProvenance before transformations: canonical shape+schema+finite little-endian float64, negative-zero normalization, SHA256 of X,Y,and concatenated raw example independent of source IDs. Draft audits all204288 examples across planes and roles and rejects overlap; each runtime rechecks its own frozen bytes, source IDs, row provenance, RNG substreams and normalized content. Manifests attest pre-freeze global disjointness without exposing opposite-plane examples/hashes. Shared immutable generator code/basis is not held-out data. Exact structural zero compositions are out of scope; floor convention is part of the raw generator. No text corpus is used.\\nRPC python_rpc_v1:handle exclusively: reset(seed), predict(X) unfitted probe, fit_center(Xtrain,Ytrain,dimension), fit_scale(), predict(mainX), predict(constantX), predict(permutedX). These are7calls/episode: reset1,unfitted1,fit_center1,fit_scale1,main_prediction1,constant_prediction1,permuted_prediction1. Setup/export/import/chunk/commit/replay counts are zero: no state transfer protocol or arrays beyond the declared bounded inline shapes. Shapes<=4096x8, <=1MiB decoded per array; training/probe/prediction production maxima fit inline. This refines the design's generic 8MiB transfer plan without dropping scientific work: reject larger values rather than invent unnecessary chunk calls. Each complete UTF8 JSON+base64+dtype/shape/byte-order+envelope+newline message<2MiB and strictly<64MiB. Preflight serializes max search/final requests/responses plus4096-row boundary and mock traces; no paths, shared files, heldout labels, baseline outputs, feedback scores or state claims in RPC. Starter model state<64MiB; candidate internals are not independently size-attested beyond the process memory bound8GiB. Exactly126 maximum searchcalls=18*7 and336 finalcalls=48*7. No replay authorized. Counter enforces the same derived totals in each evaluator.\\nCandidate outputs center[N,K-1] abs<=100 and scale[N,K-1] in[1e-4,100] in declared basis; exact keys and base64 schema validated separately from scientific decisions. Training-only polynomial-ridge center then log residual scale is the lightweight starter. Candidate fitting stages are advisory internal work, not trusted operation counters. Actual evaluator region score max_j|log(y)B-center|/scale. Prediction rows are privately interleaved across calibration/test using a deterministic permutation derived from frozen independent integration probes, identically across matched query arms; only evaluator restores role order. Calibration uses ceil((n+1)*(1-alpha)), inclusive <= ties; rank>n gives full infinite region. alpha.05,.10,.20 equal1/3. No calibration/test targets or sequential score feedback exposed. Search/final scientific validity requires independently formed regions, finite predictions, complete transcript, independent data, successful required baselines/nonvacuous structural controls, and enforced resource/isolation constraints. Search correct and final correct are declared separately but use these same scientific/integrity gates on their own full plane; neither requires superiority, conditional validity, effect sign, empirical coverage threshold or positive utility. A schema-valid candidate assertion is not evidence. Correctness does not approve a publication narrative.\\nMatched canonical controls each episode: reset->predict must be unfitted; constant training-mean features produce identical row predictions; independent cyclic derangements within calibration and test, no fixed point and at least two genuinely changed feature rows in EACH calibration/test branch, must preserve read-only input/output alignment; zero-radius point at actual predicted simplex center has continuous-noise coverage<.5. Expected feature-control loss of alignment/efficiency is empirical, no required sign and recalibrated IID coverage may remain valid. Missing/failed/vacuous controls fail completion and retain full episode worst case. Main,constant,permuted queries have matched rows, shapes,3s allowances,trained state and no label feedback; controls refit no models and add no resets. Constant or observation-independent conformal predictors remain eligible if structurally valid; no adaptivity gate is imposed. No changed-state hash or self-report gate exists.\\nEvaluator-owned baseline constructions sharing main candidate centers: unscaled max-ILR residual; simplex L-infinity; genuinely distinct Bonferroni per-coordinate quantiles alpha/K; training-only constant ILR center with unit scales; whole simplex. Baselines and controlled method scores run synchronously with bounded arrays, deadline checks every16 integration contexts,3s/method reservations; no baseline subprocess is needed and no worker telemetry invented. Candidate methods and required controls have reserved matched allowances before fitting. First method unfitted+two fitting calls, three prediction methods, nine scoring methods =13 slots at3s plus.1s overhead/slot. Native terminate.5s+kill/reap.5s+stderr reader.4s <=1.4s, no baseline-worker cleanup;4s episode overhead conservatively covers bookkeeping and cleanup including reset failure. The monotonic clock starts before numerical dependency imports; deadlines subtract startup120s search/180s final (smoke20s), reserve15s finalization, globally reserve3s reset+4s overhead per remaining episode across entire list. Conservative joint plan startup+15+episodes*(3+4+13*3.1) gives986.4s search and2465.4s final, below1200/3600 ceilings. No canonical productive-work floor exists; measured productive baseline work is recorded excluding imports/reset/cancellation/output. Smoke does not attest production completion.\\nScoring per alpha: realized JOINT coverage C, common-probe normalized simplex volume V, U=(1-V)*max(0,1-|C-(1-alpha)|/(1-alpha)). Aggregate alpha1/3 then seeds1/3 search or1/8 final within case,dimensions1/2 within family,families1/3. Balanced flattened means are equivalent. No checkpoint/decision levels. Coverage errors are absolute; IID metric uses only LN_IID and DIR_IID equal1/2; shift metric uses DIR_SHIFT. Volume and control check rate follow full hierarchy. Baseline gap is candidate aggregate utility minus max aggregate of unscaledILR/simplexLinf/Bonferroni, descriptive only. All missing/failed episode contributions fixed at utility0,error1,volume1,controls0,correct0, including missing controls/baselines, never omitted/retried/renormalized. Any unavailable baseline comparison sets entire gap=-1. Runtime is not a scalar objective. Failures retain measured actual duration only in evidence. Smoke missing unselected shift family emits fixed error1 diagnostic, not a claimed shift experiment; selected case/seed levels use identity aggregation.\\nEvidence: validated per-case per-alpha method and control outcomes in per-seed solution, merged over repeated seeds with fixed means and actual total episode duration. Conditional95% Wilson binomial intervals, two feature-defined subgroups; zero-hit volume one-sided95% bound1-.05**(1/probes) and resolution1/probes; common probes imply contexts are not independent experimental replications. Paired percentile bootstrap over independent statistical seeds with PCG64 seed62845,20000 replicates for each case/alpha baseline utility and volume difference;54 predeclared comparisons3baselines*2dimensions*3families*3alphas use Bonferroni simultaneous interval tails .05/(2*54). Overall utility uncertainty resamples statistical seed blocks keeping all cases together; feature-control paired utility differences have seed-bootstrap intervals with no sign gate. Bootstrap is finite-seed empirical uncertainty, not an exact distribution-free superiority proof, especially in3-seed search. Final eight-seed intervals remain limited; unresolved MonteCarlo-scale efficiency differences cannot substantiate superiority. Publication requires appropriate additional analysis and complete paper; executable metrics alone cannot establish literature novelty, conditional guarantees or generalization beyond the generators. Final outcomes stay sealed from search and scaffold tuning.\\n\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_training\",\n      \"search_calibration\",\n      \"search_test\",\n      \"search_integration\",\n      \"search_integrity\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_training\",\n      \"final_calibration\",\n      \"final_test\",\n      \"final_integration\",\n      \"final_integrity\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_test\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"iid_coverage_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_test\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_volume\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_test\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"shift_coverage_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_test\"\n      },\n      {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
